(SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE BOARD OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(INVESTMENT MANAGEMENT DEPARTMENT, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(SEBI/HO/IMD/DF3/P/CIR/2024/130) Tj
T*
(September 08, 2024) Tj
T*
(Master Circular for Mutual Funds - Categorization of Schemes and Risk-o-meter Guidelines) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Categorization of Equity Schemes:) Tj
T*
(\(a\) Large Cap Fund: An open-ended equity scheme investing primarily in large cap stocks. Minimum investment in equity and equity-related) Tj
T*
(instruments of large cap companies shall be 80 percent of total assets. Large cap companies are defined as the top 100 companies in terms of) Tj
T*
(full market capitalization listed on recognized stock exchanges.) Tj
T*
(\(b\) Mid Cap Fund: An open-ended equity scheme investing minimum 65 percent of total assets in equity instruments of mid cap companies. Mid cap) Tj
T*
(companies are defined as those ranked 101st to 250th in terms of full market capitalization.) Tj
T*
(\(c\) Small Cap Fund: An open-ended equity scheme investing minimum 65 percent of total assets in equity instruments of small cap companies.) Tj
T*
(Small cap companies are defined as all companies ranked from the 251st position onwards in market capitalization.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 889 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(2. Risk-o-meter Evaluation and Disclosure: Asset Management Companies \(AMCs\) shall evaluate the risk level of schemes based on the) Tj
T*
(standardized Risk-o-meter methodology on a monthly basis as of the last calendar day of the month. The updated Risk-o-meter must be published) Tj
T*
(on the AMC website and the AMFI portal on or before the 10th calendar day of the succeeding month.) Tj
T*
(3. Potential Risk Class \(PRC\) Matrix for Debt Schemes: All debt mutual fund schemes must be classified under a 3x3 Potential Risk Class Matrix) Tj
T*
(reflecting maximum interest rate risk \(measured by Macaulay duration\) and maximum credit risk \(measured by Credit Risk Value\).) Tj
T*
(Category A schemes carry low credit risk \(CRV >= 12\), Category B moderate credit risk \(CRV >= 10\), and Category C relatively high credit risk \(CRV < 10\).) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 863 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(4. Multi Cap Scheme Allocation: Multi Cap Funds are required to maintain a disciplined minimum investment of twenty-five percent) Tj
T*
(\(25 percent\) in large cap stocks, twenty-five percent in mid cap stocks, and twenty-five percent in small cap stocks at all times.) Tj
T*
(5. Flexi Cap Scheme Allocation: Flexi Cap Funds are open-ended dynamic equity schemes investing across large cap, mid cap, and small cap) Tj
T*
(stocks with a minimum overall equity investment of 65 percent of total assets, without any floor or cap across specific capitalization tiers.) Tj
T*
(6. Liquid Fund Portfolio Maturity: Liquid Funds cannot invest in debt securities having structured obligations or credit enhancements, and) Tj
T*
(shall not hold any debt security with residual maturity exceeding ninety-one calendar days \(91 days\).) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Length 873 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(7. Mandatory Liquid Assets in Liquid Funds: Liquid Funds must maintain at least twenty percent \(20 percent\) of total assets in) Tj
T*
(unencumbered liquid assets such as cash, Government securities, Treasury bills, and repo on Government securities.) Tj
T*
(8. Exit Load Structure on Liquid Funds: Liquid Funds shall levy a graded exit load on investors redeeming within seven days of investment,) Tj
T*
(ranging from 0.0070 percent on Day 1 to nil on Day 7.) Tj
T*
(9. Side-Pocketing \(Segregated Portfolio\): Creation of a segregated portfolio is permitted in case of a credit event \(downgrade to below) Tj
T*
(investment grade by a credit rating agency\) subject to prior approval of the Board of AMC and Trustees within two working days.) Tj
T*
(Yours faithfully,) Tj
T*
(\(Bhabani Prasad Pati\)) Tj
T*
(Deputy General Manager) Tj
T*
ET
